{"id":"h1-05-c4","title":"Consistent hashing","scopeHtml":"<p>Scope: hash mod N problem, ring, virtual nodes, worked example, alternatives, hot keys. Questions are still to be written.</p>","notes":[{"id":"the-problem-with-hash-mod-n","title":"The problem with hash mod N","html":"<p><strong>To spread keys over N servers, the simplest rule is server = hash(key) mod N.</strong> It works until N changes. Add or remove one server and almost every key maps somewhere new, so a cache loses nearly all its data at once.</p>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 552 68\" width=\"552\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"hash mod N: changing N moves most keys\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 34 L158 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 34 L158 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;0.251;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M248 34 L304 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M248 34 L304 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M394 34 L450 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M394 34 L450 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Key</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"203\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">hash</text><rect x=\"304\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"349\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">mod N</text><rect x=\"450\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"495\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Server</text></svg><figcaption>hash mod N: changing N moves most keys</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> Keys 0 to 11 on 3 servers (key mod 3): server 0 holds 0,3,6,9; server 1 holds 1,4,7,10; server 2 holds 2,5,8,11. Add a 4th server (key mod 4): key 4 -> 0, key 5 -> 1, key 6 -> 2, key 7 -> 3 and so on. Counting: keys that stay put are those where k mod 3 = k mod 4: only 0, 1, 2, and 12-ish repeats, so about 3 of 12 stay (25%) and 75% move. In general, going N to N+1 moves about N/(N+1) of keys.</p>\n<p><strong>Production symptom.</strong> After adding one cache node, hit ratio falls from 95% to about 20%, the database gets a cache-miss storm (thundering herd), latency spikes. Metric: cache hit ratio and DB QPS jump together.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> This is why memcached clients (libketama) and Dynamo-style stores use consistent hashing, not mod N.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> Seating by \"guest number mod tables\": adding one table reshuffles nearly everyone.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Proposing mod N for a cache cluster that must scale.</li>\n<li>Saying \"just rehash\" without cost (a cache-miss avalanche).</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"the-consistent-hashing-ring","title":"The consistent hashing ring","html":"<p><strong>Consistent hashing maps both servers and keys onto the same circle (hash ring); each key belongs to the next server clockwise.</strong> Adding or removing a server only moves the keys in one arc, about 1/N of the total on average.</p>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 650.4000000000001 68\" width=\"650.4000000000001\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Key walks clockwise to the next server\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 34 L158 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 34 L158 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;0.251;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M275.6 34 L331.6 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M275.6 34 L331.6 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M492.40000000000003 34 L548.4000000000001 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M492.40000000000003 34 L548.4000000000001 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Key</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"12\" width=\"117.60000000000001\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"216.8\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">hash position</text><rect x=\"331.6\" y=\"12\" width=\"160.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"412\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Next node clockwise</text><rect x=\"548.4000000000001\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"593.4000000000001\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Owner</text></svg><figcaption>Key walks clockwise to the next server</figcaption></figure>\n<p>Steps:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Choose a hash with a big range (for example 0 to 2^32 - 1 or 2^64 - 1).</li>\n<li>Hash each server's name or IP to a point on the ring.</li>\n<li>Hash a key; move clockwise to the first server point at or after it.</li>\n<li>Replicas: also store on the next R-1 distinct servers clockwise.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Worked ring example.</strong> Ring 0 to 99 for simplicity. Servers: A at 10, B at 40, C at 70.</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>Ring (clockwise):  A@10 ... B@40 ... C@70 ... back to A@10</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Key hash   Owner</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span> 5         A  (next clockwise point >=5 is 10)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span> 25        B  (next is 40)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span> 55        C  (next is 70)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span> 85        A  (wraps around past 99 to 10)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span> 40        B  (equal position)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Ownership ranges:  A: (70,100)+[0,10]  = 40 slots</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>                   B: (10,40]          = 30 slots</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>                   C: (40,70]          = 30 slots</span></span></code></pre>\n<p>Now add D at 55. Only keys in (40,55] move from C to D (15 slots, 15% of the ring). Keys owned by A and B do not move at all. Compare mod N, where about 75% of keys moved.</p>\n<p>Remove B: keys in (10,40] move to C (next clockwise), nothing else changes.</p>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 287.6 130\" width=\"287.6\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Adding D at 55 only affects the arc it takes over\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 34 L158 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"1.6s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 34 L158 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"1.6s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M102 96 L158 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"1.6s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 96 L158 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"1.6s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Key 50</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"74\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Key 25</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"12\" width=\"117.60000000000001\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"216.8\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">D (was C)</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"74\" width=\"117.60000000000001\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"216.8\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">B (unchanged)</text></svg><figcaption>Adding D at 55 only affects the arc it takes over</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Amazon Dynamo, Apache Cassandra (token ring), Riak, Akamai (original paper by Karger et al., 1997), and memcached client libraries.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> Houses on a circular street; each postman covers from the previous postman's house up to his own. A new postman only takes over part of one neighbour's route.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Saying keys are placed \"on the nearest server\" with no direction; the convention is the next clockwise point.</li>\n<li>Forgetting the wrap-around from the end of the ring to the start.</li>\n<li>Using a poor hash; use a uniform one (MurmurHash3, xxHash, MD5 for placement, not security).</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"the-imbalance-problem-and-virtual-nodes","title":"The imbalance problem and virtual nodes","html":"<p><strong>With few servers, random points make uneven arcs: one server may own 50% of the ring and another 10%.</strong> Also when a server dies, ALL its load falls on its single clockwise neighbour, which may then overload and die (cascade).</p>\n<p><strong>Virtual nodes (vnodes):</strong> each physical server owns many points (for example 100 to 256) on the ring. Arcs average out, and a failed server's load spreads over many neighbours.</p>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 598 68\" width=\"598\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"One physical server, many ring points\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 34 L158 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 34 L158 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M347.6 34 L403.6 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M347.6 34 L403.6 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Server A</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"12\" width=\"189.6\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"252.8\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">A#1, A#2, A#3 ... A#150</text><rect x=\"403.6\" y=\"12\" width=\"182.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"494.8\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Spread across the ring</text></svg><figcaption>One physical server, many ring points</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> 3 servers, 1 point each, positions 10, 40, 70 on a 0-99 ring: loads 40%, 30%, 30%. Now give each 3 vnodes with hashed positions:</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>A: 5, 38, 82     B: 20, 61, 90     C: 12, 47, 73</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Sorted ring: 5A 12C 20B 38A 47C 61B 73C 82A 90B</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Arcs ending at each point (previous point to this one):</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span> 5A: (90,100)+[0,5] = 15   12C: 7    20B: 8    38A: 18</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span> 47C: 9   61B: 14   73C: 12   82A: 9   90B: 8</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Totals: A = 15+18+9 = 42,  B = 8+14+8 = 30,  C = 7+9+12 = 28</span></span></code></pre>\n<p>Still not perfectly even with 3 vnodes; with 150 vnodes each, standard deviation of load drops to a few percent (rule of thumb: error roughly 1/sqrt(vnodes)). If A dies, its 9 arcs go to different successors (C, B, ...) rather than to one node.</p>\n<p><strong>Weighted capacity.</strong> Give a bigger machine more vnodes (a 64 GB node gets 2x the vnodes of a 32 GB node).</p>\n<p><strong>Decision gravity.</strong> The vnode count is hard to change once data is placed on it, because it determines token ranges and streaming; Cassandra moved its default <code>num_tokens</code> from 256 to 16 (version 4.0, with a better allocation algorithm; confirm in docs) after seeing repair and streaming costs with many vnodes. More vnodes: better balance but slower repair and more metadata. Fewer: simpler but uneven.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Cassandra <code>num_tokens</code>, Riak ring with 64 partitions, Dynamo's strategy variants.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> Instead of one big plot per farmer, each farmer owns many small plots scattered around; a farmer leaving spreads plots among many.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Forgetting vnodes, then being asked about the hot neighbour on failure.</li>\n<li>Believing vnodes fix hot KEYS; they fix unequal key RANGES only. A single hot key still lands on one server.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"lookup-and-implementation","title":"Lookup and implementation","html":"<p><strong>Keep the ring as a sorted array (or balanced tree) of (position, node); lookup is binary search, O(log V) for V total points.</strong> Add/remove is O(V) for an array or O(log V) for a tree plus the data movement.</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">import</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> bisect, hashlib</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">def</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> h</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(s: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">str</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">) -> </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">int</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">:</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">    return</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> int</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(hashlib.md5(s.encode()).hexdigest(), </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">16</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">) </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">%</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> (</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">2</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">**</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">32</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">class</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> Ring</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">:</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">    def</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> __init__</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(self, nodes, vnodes</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">=</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">100</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">):</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">        self</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">.ring </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">=</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> sorted</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">((h(</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">f</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">{</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">n</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">}</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">#</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">{</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">i</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">}</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">), n) </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">for</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> n </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">in</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> nodes </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">for</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> i </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">in</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> range</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(vnodes))</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">        self</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">.points </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">=</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> [p </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">for</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> p, _ </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">in</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> self</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">.ring]</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">    def</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> owner</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(self, key: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">str</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">) -> </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">str</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">:</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">        i </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">=</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> bisect.bisect_left(</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">self</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">.points, h(key)) </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">%</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> len</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">self</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">.points)  </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\"># wrap around</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">        return</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> self</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">.ring[i][</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">1</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">]</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">r </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">=</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> Ring([</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"A\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"B\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"C\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">])</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">print</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(r.owner(</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"user:42\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">))</span></span></code></pre>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 687.6 68\" width=\"687.6\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Lookup path\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 34 L158 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 34 L158 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;0.251;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M248 34 L304 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M248 34 L304 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M529.6 34 L585.6 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M529.6 34 L585.6 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Key</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"203\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Hash</text><rect x=\"304\" y=\"12\" width=\"225.6\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"416.8\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Binary search on sorted ring</text><rect x=\"585.6\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"630.6\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Node</text></svg><figcaption>Lookup path</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> 100 servers x 200 vnodes = 20,000 points. Binary search takes about 15 comparisons. Memory is trivial (20,000 x 16 B = 320 KB), so every client can hold the ring and route directly.</p>\n<p><strong>Alternatives.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Rendezvous (highest random weight) hashing:</strong> score = hash(key, node) for each node, pick the highest. No ring, minimal movement, O(N) per lookup; simple and good for small N (CDNs, load balancers).</li>\n<li><strong>Jump consistent hash (Google):</strong> O(log N) time, no memory, even distribution, but nodes can only be added/removed at the end (numbered buckets); good for sharding by bucket number.</li>\n<li><strong>Maglev hashing (Google):</strong> a lookup table giving near-perfect balance with minimal disruption, used in L4 load balancers.</li>\n<li><strong>Fixed slots:</strong> Redis Cluster uses 16,384 hash slots (CRC16(key) mod 16384) assigned to nodes; moving a slot moves data explicitly. Easy to reason about, not a ring.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Decision gravity.</strong> Choosing the key-to-node scheme is a near one-way door for stored data; a client-side ring requires every client to agree on membership (gossip or config). Fixed slots/logical shards (for example 1,024 logical shards on 8 machines) make later rebalancing far easier than raw hash mod machines.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Redis Cluster (slots), Cassandra/Dynamo (ring), Vitess and Instagram (logical shards), Envoy/Maglev (load balancing), Discord uses consistent hashing for routing guilds to servers.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> A phone book split into volumes; you look up the right volume first, then the name.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Not knowing that every client needs the same view of membership; stale rings cause misrouted keys.</li>\n<li>Proposing consistent hashing for a database without addressing rebalancing and replication.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"replication-data-movement-and-hot-keys","title":"Replication, data movement and hot keys","html":"<p><strong>Replication on the ring:</strong> store each key on the next R distinct physical nodes clockwise (the preference list; skip vnodes belonging to the same physical node). With R = 3, a node failure still leaves two copies.</p>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 699.5999999999999 68\" width=\"699.5999999999999\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Replicas are the next distinct nodes clockwise\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 34 L158 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 34 L158 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;0.251;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M297.2 34 L353.2 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M297.2 34 L353.2 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M492.4 34 L548.4 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M492.4 34 L548.4 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Key</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"12\" width=\"139.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"227.6\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Primary (node 1)</text><rect x=\"353.2\" y=\"12\" width=\"139.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"422.79999999999995\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Replica (node 2)</text><rect x=\"548.4\" y=\"12\" width=\"139.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"618\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Replica (node 3)</text></svg><figcaption>Replicas are the next distinct nodes clockwise</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Adding a node:</strong> the new node takes over arcs from existing nodes; those nodes stream the affected keys. Throttle streaming (for example Cassandra <code>stream_throughput_outbound</code>) so production traffic does not suffer. For caches, just let the new node warm up, or pre-warm.</p>\n<p><strong>Hot keys.</strong> A celebrity's key is one key, so hashing cannot split it. Fixes: replicate hot keys and read from any replica, add a local in-process cache (short TTL 1 to 5 s), or split a key into key#1..key#k and read a random suffix (writes update all k).</p>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> 1M reads/s on a single key and a Redis node handles 100K ops/s. Split into 16 copies key#0..key#15, each read goes to a random copy: ~62K ops/s each on 16 nodes (or 16 slots). Write cost rises 16x, acceptable for rarely-updated data.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Twitter and Facebook cache hot items with local caches and key replication. Cassandra's hinted handoff and anti-entropy repair handle temporarily missing replicas.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision gravity.</strong> Replication factor is changeable but expensive (copying data); R=3 across 3 AZs is the common default.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> Photocopying a popular book so more people can read at once.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Counting vnodes of the same physical host as separate replicas.</li>\n<li>Claiming consistent hashing solves hot keys or cascading failure alone.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"where-it-is-used-and-when-not-to","title":"Where it is used and when not to","html":"<p><strong>Use it when:</strong> servers join/leave frequently, data is distributed across many nodes, and moving everything on change is unacceptable: distributed caches, key-value stores, CDNs, sharded databases, sticky load balancing, partitioned stream processing.</p>\n<p><strong>Skip it when:</strong> the node count is fixed and small (a modulus is fine), you need range scans (hashing destroys ordering; use range partitioning with split/merge as HBase, Spanner or Bigtable do), or a directory service (lookup table) is simpler and rebalancing must be exact.</p>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 495.20000000000005 192\" width=\"495.20000000000005\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Pick the partitioning scheme\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M273.6 34 L329.6 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"1.6s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M273.6 34 L329.6 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"1.6s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M273.6 96 L329.6 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"1.6s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M273.6 96 L329.6 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"1.6s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M273.6 158 L329.6 158\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"1.6s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M273.6 158 L329.6 158\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"1.6s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"261.6\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"142.8\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Need range scans</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"74\" width=\"261.6\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"142.8\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Elastic membership, point lookups</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"136\" width=\"261.6\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"142.8\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Small fixed N</text><rect x=\"329.6\" y=\"12\" width=\"153.6\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"406.40000000000003\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Range partitioning</text><rect x=\"329.6\" y=\"74\" width=\"153.6\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"406.40000000000003\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Consistent hashing</text><rect x=\"329.6\" y=\"136\" width=\"153.6\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"406.40000000000003\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">hash mod N</text></svg><figcaption>Pick the partitioning scheme</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> Chat app: 5 cache nodes; add a 6th during growth. Consistent hashing remaps about 1/6 = 17% of keys, compared with ~83% under mod N. With 95% hit rate before, the miss rate afterwards is about 5% + 17% x 95% = 21% temporarily instead of 80+%, so the DB is hit by 4x instead of 16x.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> DynamoDB and Cassandra (ring), Memcached via libketama, Akamai and Cloudflare (hashing to cache servers), Kafka uses key hash mod partitions (fixed partition count, so adding partitions changes key mapping: a known gotcha for ordering).</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> Choosing between assigned seats on a circular table (consistent) and rows of numbered seats (mod).</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Suggesting consistent hashing for ordered/range queries.</li>\n<li>Not mentioning Kafka's partition-count change problem when asked about key ordering.</li>\n<li>Treating \"consistent hashing\" as free; clients need membership, vnodes, streaming and repair.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"summary","title":"Summary","html":"<ul>\n<li>hash mod N moves about N/(N+1) of keys when N changes; caches collapse.</li>\n<li>Consistent hashing puts servers and keys on one ring; key goes to next server clockwise; only about 1/N of keys move.</li>\n<li>Few points per server means imbalance and cascading failure; use vnodes (100 to 256 historically; fewer with smart allocation) and weights.</li>\n<li>Lookup: sorted array + binary search; replicas = next R distinct physical nodes.</li>\n<li>Alternatives: rendezvous, jump hash, Maglev, fixed slots (Redis 16,384); range partitioning for scans.</li>\n<li>It does not fix hot keys; use key splitting, local caches and replication.</li>\n</ul>"}],"questions":[]}